# Specification

## Feature Group 1 — Room Setup & Lobby

### Acceptance Criteria
1. Room creator is marked as host. Only host can start the game.
2. Joining with an invalid/empty code shows a clear error message.
3. Rooms are fully isolated (players in room A cannot see room B).
4. Lobby auto-polls every ~2 seconds.
5. Start Game button is visible, enabled only when host + 2+ players present.

### Edge Cases
- Player name empty/whitespace-only: trimmed, rejected with message.
- Room code case-insensitive.
- Duplicate participant names allowed (no uniqueness requirement).

---

## Feature Group 2 — Game Start & Drawer Flow

### Acceptance Criteria
1. Host clicking Start Game transitions room from lobby to playing.
2. First participant in the room becomes the drawer.
3. Secret word is deterministically selected from `STARTER_WORDS`.
4. Only the drawer sees the secret word. Guessers see "Waiting for drawer...".

### Edge Cases
- No second player: Start Game disabled.
- Empty/whitespace names rejected at join/create time (group 1 carryover).

---

## Feature Group 3 — Gameplay Interaction

### Acceptance Criteria
1. Drawer can draw on a canvas and clear it.
2. Drawing state is saved server-side and synced via polling.
3. Guessers submit guesses; empty/whitespace rejected.
4. Guess comparison: trimmed, case-insensitive.
5. Correct guess = +100 points. Incorrect = +0.
6. Guess history is synced to all players via polling.

### Edge Cases
- Drawer cannot submit guesses.
- Multiple correct guessers all score 100.
- Canvas state reset on new game.

---

## Feature Group 4 — Result, Restart & Final Validation

### Acceptance Criteria
1. When a correct guess is made, round ends and all players see result.
2. Result shows: secret word, final scores, full guess history.
3. Host can click Restart to return everyone to lobby.
4. Restart preserves player list, clears round state (drawing, guesses, scores).

### Edge Cases
- Restart works with same players (no duplicate re-join needed).
- Restart button visible only to host.
